:: Breakfast [simulation activity] {"position":"1400,650","size":"100,100"}
!Breakfast Time
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
It's time for breakfast. What would you like to have for breakfast today @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@? As you think about what to have you try figure out which option will give you the most energy for your errands today.

<<patient-choices "Breakfast choices" "no-eval"
	"A 24-once high protein smoothie and a 20-ounce cup of coffee | -2 | warm | red | Too much liquid all at once makes you feel really full and makes it harder to breathe | | Points+=1"
    "An 8-ounce cup of coffee, cottage cheese with fruit | 1 | warm | green | Just the right amount of food and liquid in one meal is easier for you to eat . You feel refreshed and plan to pack a protein bar as a snack for later | | Points+=1"
	"An 8-ounce cup of coffee, a glass of orange juice, two slices of toast, two fried eggs, two turkey sausage links and an apple | -2 | warm | red | It was delicious, but your body can't handle eating the way you did as a teenager anymore. All that food and liquid was filling and made it harder to breath | | Points+=1"
>>\

<<patient-next "Time to run errands" "Hallway_Out">>\

<<else>>\

@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is going to pick what he wants for breakfast. Here are his options this morning. Which do you think he'll choose? What will give him the most energy for the busy day ahead?

* A 24-once high protein smoothie and a 20-ounce cup of coffee
* An 8-ouncel cup of coffee, cottage cheese with fruit
* An 8-ounce cup of coffee, a glass of orange juice, two slices of toast, two fried eggs, two turkey sausage links and an apple
//There are no activity specific evaluations for this station//
<</if>>

<!--[[Hallway_Out]]-->


:: Dressing [simulation activity] {"position":"1600,650","size":"100,100"}
! Getting Dressed
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
Time to get dressed for the day. ''Make sure to put on your socks and shoes'' so you can run your errands.

<<patient-next "Time for breakfast!" "Breakfast">>\

<<else>>\

It's time for @@.holland;Mr Holland@@ to get dressed. Once they are done getting dressed evaluate their performance below.
//Don't forget that you can use your general controls as well to add or subtract additional energy such as if they bend over to put their shoes on//

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Getting Dressed"
" They got dressed sitting down | -1 | 1 | satAndRested | green | You're dressed and ready for breakfast | green"
"They got dressed standing up | -3 | 1 | standing | red | Even putting your clothes on for the day makes you feel winded, you wonder if you'll be able to do all your errands today | red"
>>

<</if>>

<!--[[Breakfast]]-->


:: Errands_Hub [simulation] {"position":"1600,1100","size":"100,100"}
! Whistle Stop Park
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
You've made it to Whistle Stop Park. Your errands await — grocery store, pharmacy, clinic, and more (coming soon).

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ has arrived at Whistle Stop Park. More errand stations will be added here.
<</if>>


:: Game_Over_Energy {"position":"1000,100","size":"100,100"}
! Game Over

You are very short of breath and can barely breath. You collapse on the ground and someone nearby calls an ambulance to bring you to the hospital.


:: Game_Over_Inhaler {"position":"1200,100","size":"100,100"}
! Game Over

Your heart is racing and feels like it is about to jump out of your chest. It hurts to breath and move. You curl up on the ground and a bystander calls an ambulance.


:: Good_Morning_Mr._Holland [simulation activity] {"position":"1800,450","size":"100,100"}
! Good Morning
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
Your alarm wakes you and its time to get up. You get the strangest feeling that this was the same song you woke up to yesterday morning...

Before you spend too much time thinking about the radio playlist you remember you've got a lot of things to do today. You hope that you will be able to get it all done.
<hr>\
@@.holland;Mr.Holland@@ it's time to start the day. Go ahead and get out of bed now.
    
Once you are fully standing and ready to start your day, click below to head to the bathroom to get cleaned up.

//Note that you will not be able to progress until your @@.observer;Observer@@ has evaluated your actions at this station//
    <<patient-next "Head to the Bathroom (Shower)" "Showering">>\
<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ alarm goes off, its time for him to wake up. As he listens to the song playing over the radio he gets the strangest feeling of deja-vu...
<hr>\
Tell @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ to physically get out of bed. Observe their actions carefully as they do this.
    
Once he is fully standing, click the appropriate evaluation below.
<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Getting Out of Bed"
  "He sat and rested on the edge before standing | -1 | 1 | satAndRested | green"
  "He got straight out of bed without resting | -2 | 1 | rushed | red"
>>\
<</if>>

<!--[[Showering]]-->


:: Hallway_In_Repeat [simulation activity] {"position":"1400,800","size":"100,100"}
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
!Walking back to get $yourItem
<hr>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ Go ahead and walk back to your apartment to pick up $yourItem. 

<<patient-next "Back in your apartment" "Item_Pickup">>\

<<else>>\
!Walking back to get $hisItem
<hr>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ needs to walk back inside to retrieve $hisItem. Evaluate how he moves through the building on the way back to his apartment.

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Walking up stairs"
" They took the elevator | -1 | 1 | elevator | green | Taking the elevator make is a lot easier | green"
"They took the stairs | -7 | 1 | stairs | red | You can't believe you made it up all those stairs. It felt like climbing a mountain! | red"
>>

<</if>>

<!--[[Item_Pickup]]-->


:: Hallway_Out [simulation activity] {"position":"1200,650","size":"100,100"}
!Walking out to the lobby
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
Now that you are done with breakfast it's time to start your day. Go ahead and start walking down stairs to the lobby.

<<patient-next "Time to head outside" "Wildcard_Router">>

<<else>>\
Now that @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is done with his breakfast he is ready to start his day. His first step is to walk down to the lobby. As he navigates the hallway make sure to evaluate his actions. Use the general observer controls to record if he ''sits in a chair to rest'' along the way or if he ''rushes''. 

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Walking down stairs"
" They took the elevator | -1 | 1 | elevator | green | You're glad your apartment has an elevator | green"
"They took the stairs | -3 | 1 | stairs | red | Even going down the stairs takes a lot of energy | red"
>>

<</if>>

<!--[[Wildcard_Router]]-->


:: Hallway_Out_Again {"position":"1800,800","size":"100,100"}
!Walking back downstairs
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
You have $yourItem and head back down stairs. Time to start those errands

<<patient-next "Time to head outside" "Whistle_Stop_Out">>

<<else>>\
Now that @@holland;Mr. Holland@@ has $hisItem its time to head back downstairs again. Use the general observer controls to record if he ''sits in a chair to rest'' along the way or if he ''rushes''. 

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Walking down stairs"
" They took the elevator | -1 | 1 | elevator | green | You're glad your apartment has an elevator | green"
"They took the stairs | -3 | 1 | stairs | red | Even going down the stairs takes a lot of energy | red"
>>

<</if>>

<!--[[Whistle_Stop_Out]]-->


:: Item_Pickup [simulation activity] {"position":"1600,800","size":"100,100"}
! Back Inside
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
You're back at your apartment and grab $yourItem. It's taxing having to retrace your steps, but your glad you did. It could have been dangerous going outside without $yourItem.

<<patient-next "Head back downstairs again" "Hallway_Out_Again">>

<<else>>
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is back in his apartment to pick up $hisItem. It takes a lot of energy to retrace your steps. If your were in @@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ role would you have gone back for $yourItem or kept going without it?

<</if>>

<!--[[Hallway_Out_Again]]-->


:: Lotion [simulation activity] {"position":"1800,650","size":"100,100"}
!Lotion
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
Your skin has been feeling dry lately. Perhaps some lotion would help your skin feel better. What would you like to do?

<<patient-choices "Lotion choices"
	"The lavendar scented lotion from your daughter | -2 | blue | red | It smells lovely, but strong, you immediately start coughing"
    "The generic unscented lotion | 0 | blue | green | It's nothing special, but it doesn't trigger your COPD symptoms"
	"Skip the lotion, it might trigger your COPD | 0 | blue | red | You're concerned about how your skin is going to feel today without lotion, but you have to prioritize your breathing"
>>\

<<patient-next "Time to get dressed" "Dressing">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ skin has been feeling dry. He's wondering about putting on some lotion, and if so which lotion to use, the scented or unscented.

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Applying lotion"
"They applied lotion | -1 | 2 | none | green | Your skin feels better already | green"
"They did not apply lotion | 0 | -1 | none | red | The itching is already irritating, hopefully once you start running errands you'll be distracted | red"
>>
<</if>>

<!--[[Dressing]]-->


:: PassageFooter {"position":"500,600","size":"100,100"}
<<nobr>>
<<if tags().includes("simulation") and State.variables.myRole == "observer">>
    <div id="observer-footer">
        
        <<if tags().includes("activity")>>
        /* --- DYNAMIC PASSAGE ASSESSMENTS (Injected here via <<done>> macros) --- */
		<div style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; border-top: 1px solid #333; padding-top: 5px;">Activity Specific Observations:	</div>       
		<div id="dynamic-observer-evals"></div>
        <</if>>
        
         /* --- GENERAL CONTROLS --- */
        <div style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 5px; border-top: 1px solid #333; padding-top: 5px;">General Observations:</div>
        
        <div class="eval-grid">
            <!-- Row 1 -->
            <span id="wrap-sat" class="eval-wrap green-wrap">
                <<button '<div class="eval-title">Sat & Rested</div><div class="eval-sub">+2 Energy</div>'>>
                    <<Observer_Eval "satAndRested" 2 "wrap-sat">>
                <</button>>
            </span>
            <span id="wrap-rushed" class="eval-wrap red-wrap">
                <<button '<div class="eval-title">Rushed</div><div class="eval-sub">-2 Energy</div>'>>
                    <<Observer_Eval "rushed" -2 "wrap-rushed">>
                <</button>>
            </span>
            
            <!-- Row 2 -->
            <span id="wrap-pursed" class="eval-wrap green-wrap">
                <<button '<div class="eval-title">Pursed Lip Breathing</div><div class="eval-sub">+1 Energy</div>'>>
                    <<Observer_Eval "pursedLip" 1 "wrap-pursed">>
                <</button>>
            </span>
            <span id="wrap-bent" class="eval-wrap red-wrap">
                <<button '<div class="eval-title">Bent Over</div><div class="eval-sub">-1 Energy</div>'>>
                    <<Observer_Eval "bentOver" -1 "wrap-bent">>
                <</button>>
            </span>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Bottom Row: Inhaler -->
        <div class="footer-control-row inhaler-row">
            <<if $hasInhaler>>
                <span id="wrap-inhaler" class="eval-wrap blue-wrap">
                    <<button '<div class="eval-title">Use Rescue Inhaler</div><div class="eval-sub">+2 Energy</div>'>>
                        <<Use_Inhaler>>
                    <</button>>
                </span>
            <<else>>
                <div class="gray-box">
                    <div class="eval-title" style="font-style: italic;">Rescue Inhaler</div>
                    <div class="eval-sub" style="font-style: italic;">Left at home</div>
                </div>
            <</if>>
        </div>
    </div>
<<elseif tags().includes("simulation") and State.variables.myRole == "patient">>
    <div id="patient-footer">
        <<if tags().includes("activity")>>
        <div id="patient-footer-choices"></div>
        <</if>>
        <div id="patient-footer-next"></div>
    </div>
<</if>>
<</nobr>>


:: PassageHeader {"position":"500,200","size":"100,100"}
<<nobr>>
<<if tags().includes("simulation")>>
    <<run SimApp.syncFromPlayroom()>>
    <<run State.variables.myRole = window.SimApp ? SimApp.getRole() : State.variables.myRole>>
<</if>>
<<script>>
    /* Restore role CSS class after SugarCube passage transitions */
    var role = window.SimApp && SimApp.getRole();
    if (role) {
        $("body").removeClass("role-patient role-observer").addClass("role-" + role);
    }
<</script>>
<<if tags().includes("simulation")>>
    <<set $Energy to SimApp.getVal("Energy")>>
    <<set $Inhaler to SimApp.getVal("Inhaler")>>
    <<set $Points to SimApp.getVal("Points")>>
    <<set $hasInhaler to SimApp.getVal("hasInhaler")>>

    <span id="hidden-time" class="hidden"></span>

    <<if $myRole == "observer">>
        <div id="observer-hud" class="hud-bar">
            <strong>Time:</strong>&nbsp;<span class="time-display">00:00</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
            <strong>Energy:</strong>&nbsp;<span id="energy-display"><<print $Energy>></span> / 15 &nbsp;|&nbsp;
            <strong>Inhaler:</strong>&nbsp;<span id="inhaler-display"><<print $Inhaler>></span> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
            <strong>Points:</strong>&nbsp;<span id="points-display"><<print $Points>></span>
        </div>
    <<else>>
        <div id="patient-hud" class="hud-bar">
            <strong>Time:</strong>&nbsp;<span class="time-display">00:00</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
            <strong>Status:</strong>&nbsp;<span id="patient-breathing-status">...</span> &nbsp;|&nbsp;
            <strong>Inhaler:</strong>&nbsp;<span id="patient-inhaler-status">...</span>
        </div>
    <</if>>

    <<silently>>
        /* Host broadcasts elapsed time; SimApp sync loop handles state + tether */
        <<repeat 1s>>
            <<if window.SimApp && window.SimApp.isPlayroomLoaded>>
                <<if Playroom.isHost()>>
                    <<replace '#hidden-time'>><<playtime>><</replace>>
                    <<run Playroom.setState("sharedTime", $("#hidden-time").text(), true)>>
                    <<run $(".time-display").text($("#hidden-time").text())>>
                <<else>>
                    <<run $(".time-display").text(Playroom.getState("sharedTime") || "00:00")>>
                <</if>>
            <<else>>
                <<replace '.time-display'>><<playtime>><</replace>>
            <</if>>
        <</repeat>>
    <</silently>>
<</if>>
<</nobr>>


:: PassageReady {"position":"300,200","size":"100,100"}
<<if $devmode && State.variables.myRole == "patient">>
	<<run UIBar.show()>>
<<else>>
	<<run UIBar.hide()>>
<</if>>


:: Role_Selection {"position":"1050,300","size":"100,100"}
! Choose Your Role
<hr>\
Please coordinate with your partner. One of you must be the Patient, and the other must be the Observer.

<div id="host-invite-slot"></div>

<span id="wrap-patient">
    <<button "I will be <span class='holland'>Mr. Holland</span>">>
        <<run SimApp.setRole("patient")>>
    <</button>>
</span>

<span id="wrap-observer">
    <<button "I will be <span class='observer'>the Observer</span>">>
        <<run SimApp.setRole("observer")>>
    <</button>>
</span>

<<script>>
    if (window.SimApp) {
        SimApp.mountHostInviteButton("host-invite-slot", "Show Invite QR Code");
        SimApp.refreshRoleButtons();
        if (window.roleRefreshInterval) {
            clearInterval(window.roleRefreshInterval);
        }
        window.roleRefreshInterval = setInterval(function () {
            if (passage() !== "Role_Selection") {
                clearInterval(window.roleRefreshInterval);
                return;
            }
            SimApp.refreshRoleButtons();
        }, 1000);
    }
<</script>>

<!--[[Simulation_Hub]]-->


:: Showering [simulation activity] {"position":"2000,450","size":"100,100"}
! Showering
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
First things first — you could use a shower. Walk over to the shower station.

Once you are there, what temperature will you set the water to?

<<patient-choices "Water temperature"
  "Hot Water | -4 | hot | red | All the steam from the hot water makes it hard to breathe! But at least you are clean."
  "Warm Water | -1 | warm | green | The warm water is soothing and doesn't stress your lungs."
  "Cold Water | -2 | cold | red | The sudden shock of the cold water makes you gasp for air!"
>>\

<<patient-next "Time to brush your teeth" "Teeth_Brushing">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at the shower. Observe how he sets the water temperature and how his breathing responds.

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Showering"
  "He showered sitting down | 0 | 1 | satAndRested | green | You're glad your daughter convinced you to buy the shower chair, it certainely makes things easier in the morning | green"
  "He showered standing up | -2 | 1 | standing | red | The day has barely begun and you're already starting to feel a little winded | red"
>>\
<</if>>

<!--[[Teeth_Brushing]]-->


:: Simulation_Hub [simulation briefing] {"position":"1200,450","size":"100,100"}
! Tutorial & Controls Practice
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
!! Welcom to the game @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ 
This is what your user interface will look like when you start the game. At the top of your screen you will see your heads up display (HUD) showing the time elapsed in the simulation, your current work of breathing, and whether you have your rescue inhaler with you.

The clock is running now so you can see the real HUD in action. It will reset to zero when you start the actual simulation.

If you have your rescue inhaler with you, during the simulation you may demonstrate correct inhaler technique to your @@.observer;Observer@@ and they will add some energy. Don't forget to keep track of how many times you have used it during the simulation. You can only use it 6 times per day according to the doctor.

For now, use the <strong><u>Practice Activity</u></strong> button at the bottom of your screen to try a sample action and see how it impacts your work of breathing.
<hr>\
    <<patient-next "Begin Practice Activity" "Tutorial_Jumping_Jacks""reset">>
<<else>>\
!! Welcome to the game @@.observer;Observer@@!
You will be following along with @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ and assessing how well he conserves his energy as he goes about his day. 
This is what your user interface will look like when you start the game. At the top of your screen you will see your heads up display (HUD) showing:
*The time elapsed in the simulation. //Don't worry about the clock ticking right now it will reset after these tutorial pages when we start the actual simulation//
*@@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ current energy
*If @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ has is inhaler
*How many points he has earned

The clock is running now so you can see the real HUD in action. It will reset to zero when you start the actual simulation.

!!! How the Simulation Works
* ''Hidden Stats:'' The student playing @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ cannot see their exact energy or inhaler uses. They will only see a rough estimate of their breathing status.
* ''Gaining Energy:'' They can use energy-conserving techniques to regain energy.
* ''Inhaler Use:'' They can use their albuterol rescue inhaler to regain energy, but make sure your partner actually demonstrates correct technique for it to count.
* ''Losing Energy:'' They will lose energy if they rush, don't take breaks, or bend over (which compresses their lungs and makes it harder to breathe).
* ''Button Limits:'' The assessment buttons in the footer can only be used once per activity, but they will reset at the next station.

!!! Practice Area
Try clicking the buttons at the bottom of the screen in ''General Observations'' right now to see how they affect @@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ energy level!

For some activities, you will be provided with different options that automatically assign points and energy based on how @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ performed.

Once you feel comfortable with the controls and @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is comfortable with the practice activities, they will start the simulation from their screen.
<</if>>

<!--[[Tutorial_Jumping_Jacks]]-->


:: Start {"position":"800,400","size":"200,200"}
<div class="center-heading1">@@.holland;Mr Holland's@@ Grand Day Out</div>\
<div class="center-heading3">Version <<print Story.title.replace(/^COPD simulation\s+/i, "")>></div>\
<hr>\
<div class="center-heading2">An interactive augmented reality simulation by Robin Parker, MSN, RN, PCCN</div>\
<div class="center-heading3">Cursor AI was used to assist with coding and debugging</div>\
<nobr>\
<div id="loading-overlay">Loading multiplayer services...</div>\
<div id="connect-container" class="hidden">\
    <<button "Connect to Multiplayer">>\
        <<run SimApp.connect()>>\
    <</button>>\
</div>\
</nobr>\
Welcome to this live nursing simulation. You will need a partner to complete this activity. 
Before we begin please review the briefing below.
<hr>\
!! Briefing
Today you and your partner will be living a day in the life of @@.holland;Mr. Bernard Holland@@, a 75-year-old male with COPD. He is 60-pack-year smoker who is currently trying to quit. He does not wear home oxygen, though he does often have to stop to catch his breath after walking for more than a few minutes on level ground.

!!! Home Medications
* Albuterol sulfate rescue inhaler: 1-2 Puffs PRN for wheezing/shortness of breath every 4 hours *(Not to exceed 6 puffs per day!)*
* Formoterol/budesonide maintenance inhaler: 1 puff, BID
* Tiotropium maintenance inhaler: 1 puff, once daily
* Theophylline ER: 400mg, PO once daily in the morning
* Nicotine patch: 21mg, transdermal, once daily in the morning
<br>
!!! Your goal
Your goal  is to accomplish as many tasks during your day as possible. This is a ''timed simulation''. You and your partner will be competing against your classmates!

Each activity your team completes will earn you points, with some activities being worth more points than others.

At the end of the simulation the winning team will be determined by the amount of points earned during the simulation. In the event of a tie, the fastest time will be used to break the tie.

!!! Roles
* @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@: In this role you will be making choices about what activities to complete and how to perform those activities to conserve your energy. 
* @@.observer;The Observer@@:  In this role you will be evaluating  @@.holland;Mr. Holand's@@ performance throughout his daily routine. You will be adding and deducting energy based on his performance, along with providing cues on what to do next.

!!! Energy Management
* @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ will start with @@color:green;10 energy@@. and can have a maximum of @@color:green;15 energy@@.
* Each task you perform will cost energy, with certain tasks costing more than others. 
* When you use energy conservation techniques or use your rescue inhaler @@.observer;The Observer@@ will be able to @@color:green; add energy@@. Conversly not using good breathing technique can result in @@color:red; subtracting energy@@
* If @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ reaches @@color:red; 0 energy@@, its game over and you will have to return to ''room 8220 for debriefing.''

!!! Today's Itinerary
The game will start with  @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ getting out of bed in the morning, which will start the clock for the simulation. After that, you’ll need to shower, brush your teeth, get dressed, along with other activities of daily living.

It’s coming up on the end of the month and @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ has a lot of errands on his to-do list including:
* Go to the grocery store.
* Pick up his prescriptions ''(He is almost out of his maintenance medications, fortunately he still has an extra rescue inhaler!)''.
* Visit the pulmonary rehab clinic.
* Go to the toy store to buy a gift for his granddaughter's 7th birthday tomorrow.

!!! Augmented Reality Approach
* To give you an understanding of what it is like to live with a chronic illness the student playing the role of  @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ will need to act out many of the activities as if you are actually doing them. For example putting on your shoes will require actually putting on your shoes, while folding laundry will require you to fold a pile of laundry.
* @@.observer;The Observer@@ will assign energy additions or substractions based on @@.holland;Mr. Holand's@@ actual physical performance of that task.
* Once you connect to the multiplayer lobby the student playing the role of @@.holland;Mr. Holand@@ wil be controlling the pace of the game and moving from activity station to activity station. The game will tell you where to go next or it may give you options to chose from.
*Meanwhile the @@.observer;The Observer@@ be provided specific scoring buttons for each task.

!! To start the game 
* Have one player click the "Connect to Multiplayer" button below. This will connect you to the game lobby.
* Once in the game lobby click the <strong><u>Invite</u></strong> button. This will give you a QR code for your partner to pair up and form a team.. If you leave the lobby before your partner joins, the host can tap <strong><u>Show Invite QR Code</u></strong> on the role selection screen to display it again.
* Once you've both joined the 1st player can then click the <strong><u>Launch</u></strong> button to enter the briefing area to learn the controls.
//Don't bother spending time customizing your avatar or player names. These won't be used in the game//

<!--[[Role_Selection]]-->
<!--[[Waiting_Room]]-->


:: StoryCaption {"position":"300,400","size":"100,100"}
<<if $devmode && State.variables.myRole == "patient">>
	<<run UIBar.show()>>
!!Dev Mode

<details>
    <summary><strong>Score & Status</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Energy">Energy: <<numberbox "$Energy" $Energy>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Points">Points: <<numberbox "$Points" $Points>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Inhaler">Inhaler Uses: <<numberbox "$Inhaler" $Inhaler>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="win">Win State:
    <<listbox "$win" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
   </details>

   <details>
    <summary><strong>Techniques</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="satAndRested">Sat/Rested: <<numberbox "$satAndRested" $satAndRested>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="pursedLip">Pursed Lip: <<numberbox "$pursedLip" $pursedLip>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="rushed">Rushed: <<numberbox "$rushed" $rushed>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="bentOver">Bent Over: <<numberbox "$bentOver" $bentOver>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="stairs">Stairs: <<numberbox "$stairs" $stairs>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="elevator">Elevator: <<numberbox "$elevator" $elevator>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="standing">Standing: <<numberbox "$standing" $standing>></span>
   </details>

  <details>
    <summary><strong>Locations & Events</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="errandsRun">Errands Run: <<numberbox "$errandsRun" $errandsRun>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="wildRoll">Wild Roll: <<numberbox "$wildRoll" $wildRoll>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="wildCarded">Wild Carded:
    <<listbox "$wildCarded" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedHallway">Visited Hallway:
    <<listbox "$visitedHallway" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedGrocery">Visited Grocery:
    <<listbox "$visitedGrocery" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedPharmacy">Visited Pharmacy:
    <<listbox "$visitedPharmacy" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedToyStore">Visited Toy Store:
    <<listbox "$visitedToyStore" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedClinic">Visited Clinic:
    <<listbox "$visitedClinic" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
   </details>

 <details>
    <summary><strong>Inventory</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="yourItem">Your Item: <<textbox "$yourItem" $yourItem>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hisItem">His Item: <<textbox "$hisItem" $hisItem>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasInhaler">Has Inhaler:
    <<listbox "$hasInhaler" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasMedications">Has Meds:
    <<listbox "$hasMedications" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasToy">Has Toy:
    <<listbox "$hasToy" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
 </details>

    ---
//**Passage Navigator**//
    Passage Name:
    <<textbox "_jumpTarget" "">>
    <<button "Jump To Passage (team)">>
        <<if Story.has(_jumpTarget)>>
            <<run SimApp.goToSharedPassage(_jumpTarget)>>
        <<else>>
            <<run UI.alert("Error: Passage '" + _jumpTarget + "' does not exist.")>>
        <</if>>
    <</button>>

    <<button "Sync from Playroom">>
        <<run SimApp.syncFromPlayroom(); SimApp.refreshDevCaptionUI(); SimApp.updateHud()>>
    <</button>>
    ---
<<script>>
setTimeout(function () {
    if (window.SimApp && State.variables.devmode) {
        SimApp.wireDevCaptionControls();
    }
}, Engine.minDomActionDelay);
<</script>>
<</if>>


